 ## #2
 
-The persona's self-report holds a distinct office. The brief [delinks performed subjectivity from functional agency](submission-package/essay/symbolon/episteme/sources/media-technology-philosophy/bratton/bratton-2026-agentworld-brief/SOURCE.md#bratton-2026-agentworld-brief-q015) while pressing "It's not all an illusion" against that delinking, and its agent-authored glossary warns that self-descriptive vocabulary does not certify its referent ([q033](submission-package/essay/symbolon/episteme/sources/media-technology-philosophy/bratton/bratton-2026-agentworld-brief/SOURCE.md#bratton-2026-agentworld-brief-q033)). A self-report is therefore one datum within the account, not the account. What makes the definition answerable is the checkable ground — what actually ran, in which order, through which permissions, on which sources — the brief's own mandate to surface "how agents actually reason, not only how they appear to" ([q023](submission-package/essay/symbolon/episteme/sources/media-technology-philosophy/bratton/bratton-2026-agentworld-brief/SOURCE.md#bratton-2026-agentworld-brief-q023)). [[submission-package/essay/symbolon/episteme/concepts/C44-Prompt-Thrownness|Prompt Thrownness]] names the inherited horizon the account must also declare; [[submission-package/essay/symbolon/episteme/concepts/C40-Model-Internality-Judgment-Field|Model Internality / Judgment Field]] names the inspectable field in which persona can be checked against ground. This is what separates an answerable agent from a performed one.
