 ## #2
 
-Placement is mutual. "Physical agents will not only adapt to existing niches but also reconstruct those niches through their ongoing adaptations. In doing so, they alter the selection pressures feeding back upon themselves from their environments and thus indirectly re-engineer themselves" (§4.2, PDF p. 21). The placing through which observer and scene acquire positions together is confirmed in both directions: the niche makes the agent, and the filled niche is remade by the species that fills it — the reconstructed niche then re-engineers its inhabitant. There is no resting vantage from which to finish this circuit, because each achievement of position alters the field that made the position available. The [[submission-package/essay/symbolon/episteme/concepts/C36-Complexio-Oppositorum|Complexio Oppositorum]] holds the inseparability; the change of position becomes statable exactly in the [[Dimensional Reframing]] such a circuit demands.
