 ## #3
 
-Living symbol and idol can be visibly identical; the difference appears when an encounter resists the image. In a living relation the resistance can revise interpretation and valuation: the source corrects the profile, the criterion under the persona is reached and changed. Under possession, the image fixes in advance what the source may disclose — the witness must be ignorant, unfaithful, corrupt or unreal because the account cannot be wrong. The technical form is the operational profile A20 derives, and the agentworld generalises it past the single score: a profile selects access; the selected circumstances shape the person's behaviour; the behaviour returns as further evidence for the profile. If revision can change only the person's record and never the criterion, the representation's causal efficacy protects its claim to truth — the change of office the [[Living Symbol / Idol]] concept qualifies, insulated as a [[submission-package/essay/symbolon/episteme/concepts/C27-Protected-Account-Occupied-Zero-Source-Claim|Protected Account]]. Q27's deepfake passage adds the second-order break: the sign can counterfeit its source relation and then make an authentic record dismissible as another fabrication; the [[Counterfeit Symbolon]] defines the fabricated slash, and provenance must participate in the encounter because a convincing image cannot certify the relation it claims to carry. At population scale this stabilised confusion is the film [A32′](A32-prime-The-Mirror-Is-a-Film.md) completes.
